/*
This example script demonstrates ways to call scripts and pass
parameters to and from a called script.

The script calls '1-generator.ces' script in order to generate
a waveform signal and '1-estimator.ces' script to estimate
signal parameters. In addition, '2-noise.ces' script will also
be called from '1-generator.ces'.

A call of scripts is performed with the help of 'call' function
that reads a script file and executes the script. A called
script has its own variable context that does not interfere
with the context of the calling script. The 'call' function
passes the specified parameters between variable contexts of
calling and called scripts.

The 'call' function accepts a path of script to be called as
string parameter that should specify either an absolute or
relative file path. If a path is relative, the 'call' function
firstly attempts to read the script file in the directory
containing the calling script. If it fails, the 'call' function
uses 'search paths' in order to find the required script file.

A file path of the top-level script has to be specified with
the help of a respective CSE VI before CSE starts executing the
script. Search paths can be defined before execution of a
top-level script as well as they can be defined in a script
with the help of 'SearchPath' function. A called script inherits
search paths from its caller. A file path of a script can be
retrieved with the call of 'ScriptPath' function.
*/

/* Define search path(s) if the current script has no specified file path */
if ( ScriptPath() == "") {
  path = FileGetAppPath(9);  // CE Project directory
  path = FileBuildPath(path, "Example Scripts/call scripts");
  SearchPath(path);          // set script search path
}

Form = "sine";  // signal form: "sine","square","triangle"
A  = 3.5;       // amplitude
F  = 8.65;      // signal frequency
Ph = 0;         // initial phase
DC = 0.5;       // DC value
Fs = 1000;      // sampling frequency
Ns = 1000;      // number of samples
NA = 0.7;       // noise apmlitude
NK = "uniform"; // noise kind: "uniform","gaussian","random"

/*
Call the script to generate a waveform signal.
The 'waveform' variable will be implicitly created after the called script completed.
Non-specified parameters like Ns (number of samples) will get
the default values. See the called script for details.
*/
err = call( "1-generator.ces",
                  "Form >> Form",
                  "Fs   >> Fs",
                  "A    >> A",
                  "F    >> F",
                  "DC   >> DC",
                  "NA   >> Noise",
                  "waveform << Signal");
if (err) return;

/* display waveform */
WFGraph(0, waveform, 0, 1/Fs, "Signal","Generated Signal");

/* Call the script to estimate waveform signal parameters */
frq = rms = ave = 0;
err = call( "1-estimator.ces",
                  "waveform >> Signal & Fs >> Fs",
                  "frq << F & rms << RMS & ave << AVE");
if (err) return;

Report = sform(	"Estimated parameters of a %s signal:\n"
		"RMS = %.4f\n"
		"AVE = %.4f\n"
		"Frequency = %.2f"
		, Form, rms, ave, frq );
MsgBox( Report );
